WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:03.335
 Jason, Seth, congratulations.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:06.606
Your boarding axes have earned
you a spot in our finale.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.207
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:10.977
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.078
That weapon is--

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:18.151
Blackbeard's infamous cutlass.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.021
Good luck.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.756
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.759 line:7%
[foreboding music]

00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:29.628
SETH: I'm feeling pretty excited
to be back in my home forge.

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:32.598
Today I'm going to be making
two different kinds of Damascus.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:36.069
I've never made a weapon
of this caliber this size,

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:39.839
and I've never done any kind
of knuckle bow or D-guard.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.974
I have a huge chunk
of steel here.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.543
That's for sure.

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:48.547
The judges really hit on the
handle and weight distribution.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.483
I'm going to make sure
the handles aren't too big

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.084
but they're not too
small, because there

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:55.522
will be multiple operators.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.524 line:7%
[heavy metal music]

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.559
JASON: So it's start
of day one, and I

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:03.329
cannot wait to get started on
Blackbeard's legendary cutlass.

00:01:03.395 --> 00:01:06.199
I've never built anything
like this, not even close,

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.402
so I'm going to be making
most of it up as I go along.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.836
Plan for day one--

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.640
I definitely want to have the
blade shaped out, formed out.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:14.808
I want to have the fullers done.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.409
I want to have the
rough grind done.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:19.278
So I'm using this guillotine
tool to try and get

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.748
these fullers forged in.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.282
I have no press,
no power hammers.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.585
Uh, my power hammer is--

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:26.819
look at that, huh?

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.121
This is the problem.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:29.456
You get an arm like
that and one like that.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:35.027
SETH: I did the heat treat.

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.463
Today, I want to
work on the handle.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:40.132
I've never put a guard
together like this ever.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:43.502
Getting all the measurements
right is just guesswork.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:46.205
I'm doing Damascus for
all the handle pieces.

00:01:46.271 --> 00:01:48.841
I want all of it to be uniform.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.276
If something's out
of place or out

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.712
of whack or out of
tune or out of twist,

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.480
it's not going to work.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:57.016
It's a lot of steel to
be putting on a handle.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.351
Yeah.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.852
I hope that the amount
of steel on the weapon

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:01.554
won't make it too heavy.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.256 line:0%
Blackbeard just might as
well throw it in the water

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.992 line:7%
and use it as an anchor.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.194 line:7%
JASON: It's day three.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:11.998 line:0%
The blade is out of tempering,
looking really good.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.767 line:0%
But there is a ton
of work to do today,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.403 line:0%
and it's going to be
forging the handle parts.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.539
So I'm going to go through
my scrap pile to find steel.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.209
It's probably just going to
be some kind of mild steel.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:27.279
And the plan is to take
it one piece at a time

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:31.250
and forge it as if I was
forging a jigsaw puzzle.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.119
The guard bone's connected
to the knuckle bow

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:36.088
bone's connected to the
rear [inaudible] bone.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.256
It's going to be a--

00:02:37.322 --> 00:02:39.625
an interesting forging process.

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:42.327 line:0%
Even though it's going
to be cheesy and campy,

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:46.899 line:0%
I'm making the clamshell
guard look like clamshell.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:50.836
This morning, uh, got a lot
of grinding to do on the blade

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:52.471
and shaping the handle.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.675
I want to do a
robust edge on it.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:59.545
I want to keep it thick so it
doesn't get broke up so easily.

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:02.248
I've bent my guard out to
get the heat treat right,

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.417
and now I've got
to bend it back in.

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.619
We'll see how good my temper is.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:07.420
[clanking]

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:08.454
Ooh.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.222
[bleep]

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:12.625
I just broke my knuckle bow.

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:15.895
This is not how to get
into the final day.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.196
It's hard.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.066
I think it's going to be
a pretty good struggle

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.934
trying to get it together.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:26.138
What I'm going to do is
shorten out my knuckle bow,

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:28.074
get it into--

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.276
position to where I need it.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:34.013
Maybe breaking it was
a blessing in disguise.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.915
I got to rework the
knuckle bow the way I

00:03:35.981 --> 00:03:38.517
wanted it, to make it prettier.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.386
I like it.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.887
My sword is all together.

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:43.656
It's all one piece now.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.457
It's a cutlass.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:47.193
It's Blackbeard's cutlass.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.296
Heavy-- ish.

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:53.299
DOUG: Bladesmiths, to test
the lethality of your cutlass,

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.767
I'm going to inflict
lethal wounds

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.836
on these ballistic dummies.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:57.670
Jason, you're up first.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.371
You ready?

00:03:58.471 --> 00:03:59.605
 I sure hope so, Doug.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.107
 Let's do this.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:04.710
[heavy metal music]

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:08.648
[blade impact sounds]

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:26.164
All right, Jason.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.934
You've got a very
big handle here.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.502
But at least it's
got the swells.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.437
It's got an indexing to
where I hold onto it,

00:04:31.503 --> 00:04:33.038
I can tell where the edge is.

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:36.409
The weight that you have in this
weapon is so light in a sense

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.744
that I can wield it
even around here.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:41.747
You cut the clavicle into
the ribs, all the way

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:43.382
through the lungs.

00:04:43.448 --> 00:04:46.952
And definitely, it will kill.

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:48.320
 All I ever wanted to hear.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:49.421
Made my day.

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:50.656
DOUG: Seth, you're up next.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:51.223
You ready?

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.159
 Let's get some.

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:57.697
[heavy metal music]

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:05.071
[blade impact sounds]

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:20.986
 [chuckles]

00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:22.588
DOUG: All right, Seth.

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:25.691
Your sword is forward-heavy
without a balance coming back.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.393
I don't know whose shoulder's
going to hurt more,

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.028
the dummy's or mine.

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:31.730
But your weapon, sir, will kill.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:32.465
 Thank you.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.670
 To test the strength and
durability of your swords,

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.439
I'll be chopping
through these bones

00:05:40.505 --> 00:05:42.007
and then attacking that peg leg.

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:45.478
Now, remember, this test is
not about when your blades

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:46.845
do to these targets.

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.448
It's about what these
targets do to your blades.

00:05:49.548 --> 00:05:50.616
Jason, you're up.
You ready?

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:51.250
 Nope.

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:52.085
[chuckles]

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:54.087
[sighs]

00:05:56.522 --> 00:06:02.595
[blade impact sounds]

00:06:15.407 --> 00:06:18.443
 The balance of your
weapon is really nice,

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.379
which is surprising
because you've made

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:22.781
a two-handed cutlass.

00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:26.519
Your blade held up very well,
except for the one little chip.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:27.686
And it's not even a chip.

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:28.587
It's a roll.

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.089
So it didn't blow out.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:31.157
Good job.

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:31.923
 Thank you, Dave.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:32.792
DAVE: All right.

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:33.759
Seth, are you ready?

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:36.094
 Yes, sir.

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:39.999
[blade impact sounds]

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:55.047
DAVE: All right, Seth.

00:06:55.113 --> 00:06:58.017
First up, this thing's a beast.

00:06:58.084 --> 00:07:02.755
It is probably a pound heavier
than your competitor's sword.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:06.559
Your blade-- I can run
my fingernail down this.

00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:09.128
I can see a couple
of glinting spots,

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:10.563
but it really didn't
take any damage.

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:14.867
DOUG: All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:17.236
Let's find out if
there's any edge left.

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:20.339
This is the rope cut
and pirate sail slash.

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:21.807
To test the edge
of your cutlass,

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:24.410
I will cut this rope,
which will raise the sail,

00:07:24.476 --> 00:07:26.846
and then I will slash the sail.

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:29.281
This is all about
what your sword

00:07:29.347 --> 00:07:31.717
will do to the sail and rope.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:33.019
Jason, you're up first.
Ready?

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:33.786
 Yes, sir.

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:42.128
[blade impact sounds]

00:07:51.603 --> 00:07:53.573
DOUG: All righty, Jason.

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:57.810
Your edge cut through the rope
easily and cuts with every part

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.280
that the edge met
on this pirate sail.

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:04.450
Overall, sir, your
sword will cut.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.018
 Awesome.

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.253
DOUG: Seth, how you feeling?

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:07.986
 Feeling good.

00:08:08.053 --> 00:08:08.854
Let's go.

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:09.589
 Let's do this.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:19.232
[blade impact sounds]

00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:31.977
All right, Seth.

00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:34.213
What are the chances you
find a very dull spot

00:08:34.279 --> 00:08:35.714
on the first cut on the rope?

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:39.051
But on the second cut, it found
another spot that was sharp.

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:42.921
But on the sail, working
a heavy sword like this

00:08:43.022 --> 00:08:43.723
affects my cuts.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:51.563
 Jason, Seth, the judges
have tested your weapons,

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:53.465
and they've made
a final decision.

00:08:53.565 --> 00:08:55.601
And the new "Forged
in Fire" champion is--

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.106
Jason, congratulations.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:03.643
You're the new "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:03.743 --> 00:09:06.879
Seth, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:09.849
DOUG: Seth, your weapon
was significantly heavier,

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:12.484
and it had a stout edge
that underperformed

00:09:12.584 --> 00:09:13.752
on the sharpness test.

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:16.021
For that reason, we're
sending you home.

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:19.625
WIL: Seth, please
surrender your blade.

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:21.026
SETH: No regrets, man.

00:09:21.126 --> 00:09:23.662
I think I made an
exceptional blade,

00:09:23.728 --> 00:09:25.731
but it is what it is, you know?

00:09:25.798 --> 00:09:26.832
Elimination's elimination.

00:09:26.932 --> 00:09:28.500
That's the name of the game.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.337
I'm proud of myself,
but I don't feel as good

00:09:31.403 --> 00:09:32.805
as I would have if I had won.

00:09:36.441 --> 00:09:37.642
WIL: Jason, congratulations.

00:09:37.709 --> 00:09:39.811
You are our new "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:39.911 --> 00:09:42.247
and that's a title that comes
with a bundle of bullion

00:09:42.314 --> 00:09:44.150
that's worth 10 grand.

00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:45.317
How are you feeling right now?

00:09:45.417 --> 00:09:48.354
 [chuckles] I mean, come on.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.688
That's incredible.

00:09:49.754 --> 00:09:52.390
 Please, present your
blade to the judges.

00:09:52.457 --> 00:09:53.358
JASON: What?

00:09:53.425 --> 00:09:55.794
"Forged in Fire" champion?

00:09:55.894 --> 00:09:57.997
I don't know how to respond
because I never expected

00:09:58.097 --> 00:10:01.166
to be here, saying that.

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:01.967
I don't know.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:04.703
[laughs] What?

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.271
What do you want from me?

00:10:06.371 --> 00:10:09.742
[symphonic metal music]

